<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rajasthan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rajasthan is the largest state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> by area, in the north-west of the country on the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>. It includes the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thar-desert">Thar Desert</a> west of the Aravalli Range and more fertile land to the south-east. Long divided among <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> kingdoms, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> under British protection, it was formed in stages between 1948 and 1956 by merging those states, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaipur">Jaipur</a> as its capital.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rajasthan.jpg" alt="Rajasthan" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thar_Khuri.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
